We need to differentiate the function y = 2^{sin x}. Use the chain rule. Let u = sin x. Then dy/dx = d/dx (2^u) = 2^u * ln 2 * du/dx. Compute du/dx = cos x. So dy/dx = 2^{sin x} * ln 2 * cos x. Provide final answer in boxed format.
